The famous book Al Qanoon Fi Tib was written by Abu Ali Sina (Avicenna / Ibn Sina). Below are key facts about this masterpiece:
· Author & background: It is the enduring medical encyclopedia compiled by Persian physician-philosopher Avicenna (Ibn Sina, 980–1037 CE).
· Completion date: The Canon was finished in 1025 and originally written in Arabic.
· Structure: The work is divided into five books:
· Book 1 – general medical principles;
· Book 2 – Materia medica (~800 individual drugs);
· Book 3 – diseases of specific organs;
· Book 4 – general diseases (fevers, poisons, etc.);
· Book 5 – formulary of compound remedies (~650 formulations).
· Enduring influence: Translated into Latin in the 12th century, it served as the standard medical textbook in Europe and the Islamic world for over 500 years, remaining in use through the 17th century.
